Cloud computing is the delivery of computing services over the internet ("cloud"). This service includes 
  1. Storage(saving file)
  2. Processing power(Running software, websites, Or AI models)
  3. Networking
  4. Software application

Key Features
  - On-demand:- Use resources when you need them.
  - Scalable:- Easily up|down based on demand
  - Pay-as-you-go:- Pay only for what you use
  - Accessible Anywhere:- requires only an internet connection.

☁️ Types  of Cloud Services
1. IaaS:- (Infrastructure as a Service)- renting a virtual server, 
   e.g, hosting a website on AWS(EC2/S3), hosting ERPs, CRMs, or internal company apps,
2. SaaS: (Software as a Service) - software service delivered to the user via app/web
   e.g, Netflix, Google Drive, Google Workspace, Microsoft 365
3. PaaS:- (Platform as a Service)- tools to build and host applications
